# CoCIS Smart Control & Monitoring System - Room 1 (Learning Guide)

Generated: 2026-10-24 21:39:50
Target: ESP32-S3 DevKitC-1, ESP-IDF via PlatformIO, Wokwi Simulation

## Project structure
D:\cocis-smart-system\room1\
  |-- platformio.ini
  |-- wokwi.toml
  |-- diagram.json
  \-- src\
       \-- main.c

## File by file explanation

### platformio.ini
Purpose: Tells PlatformIO what board/framework to use.
`ini
[env:esp32-s3-devkitc-1]
platform = espressif32
board = esp32-s3-devkitc-1
framework = espidf
monitor_speed = 115200
`
- [env:...] - defines an environment
- platform = espressif32 - Espressif chips platform
- board = esp32-s3-devkitc-1 - exact dev board (matches Wokwi)
- framework = espidf - use ESP-IDF (NOT Arduino)
- monitor_speed - baud rate for serial monitor

### src/main.c
`c
#include <stdio.h>
#include <stdbool.h>
#include \"freertos/FreeRTOS.h\"
#include \"freertos/task.h\"
#include \"driver/gpio.h\"
#include \"esp_err.h\"
#include \"esp_log.h\"

#define PIR_GPIO        GPIO_NUM_4
#define LIGHT_GPIO      GPIO_NUM_2
#define OCCUPANCY_TIMEOUT_MS 15000
#define SAMPLE_PERIOD_MS     200

static const char *TAG = \"ROOM1\";

static void room1_task(void *arg)
{
    bool occupied = false;
    TickType_t last_motion = 0;

    while (1) {
        int motion = gpio_get_level(PIR_GPIO);
        TickType_t now = xTaskGetTickCount();

        if (motion) {
            last_motion = now;
            if (!occupied) {
                occupied = true;
                gpio_set_level(LIGHT_GPIO, 1);
                ESP_LOGI(TAG, \"Motion detected -> OCCUPIED, LIGHT ON\");
            }
        } else if (occupied) {
            uint32_t idle_ms = (now - last_motion) * portTICK_PERIOD_MS;
            if (idle_ms >= OCCUPANCY_TIMEOUT_MS) {
                occupied = false;
                gpio_set_level(LIGHT_GPIO, 0);
                ESP_LOGI(TAG, \"No motion for %u ms -> VACANT, LIGHT OFF\",
                         (unsigned)OCCUPANCY_TIMEOUT_MS);
            }
        }

        vTaskDelay(pdMS_TO_TICKS(SAMPLE_PERIOD_MS));
    }
}

void app_main(void)
{
    gpio_config_t pir_config = {
        .pin_bit_mask = (1ULL << PIR_GPIO),
        .mode = GPIO_MODE_INPUT,
        .pull_up_en = GPIO_PULLUP_DISABLE,
        .pull_down_en = GPIO_PULLDOWN_ENABLE,
        .intr_type = GPIO_INTR_DISABLE,
    };
    ESP_ERROR_CHECK(gpio_config(&pir_config));

    gpio_config_t light_config = {
        .pin_bit_mask = (1ULL << LIGHT_GPIO),
        .mode = GPIO_MODE_OUTPUT,
        .pull_up_en = GPIO_PULLUP_DISABLE,
        .pull_down_en = GPIO_PULLDOWN_DISABLE,
        .intr_type = GPIO_INTR_DISABLE,
    };
    ESP_ERROR_CHECK(gpio_config(&light_config));

    gpio_set_level(LIGHT_GPIO, 0);

    ESP_LOGI(TAG, \"CoCIS Room 1 controller started\");
    ESP_LOGI(TAG, \"PIR=GPIO%d LIGHT=GPIO%d timeout=%d ms\",
             PIR_GPIO, LIGHT_GPIO, OCCUPANCY_TIMEOUT_MS);

    xTaskCreate(room1_task, \"room1_task\", 4096, NULL, 5, NULL);
}
`

Explanation:
- app_main() runs once at boot - initializes hardware, logs, creates task
- gpio_config() configures pins
- xTaskCreate() creates FreeRTOS task (runs in background)
- room1_task() loops forever: reads PIR every 200ms
- State machine: occupied/vacant (only log on transition)
- Timeout uses xTaskGetTickCount() (FreeRTOS ticks) to track idle time
- vTaskDelay() yields CPU, not blocking

### wokwi.toml
`	oml
[wokwi]
version = 1
firmware = '.pio/build/esp32-s3-devkitc-1/firmware.bin'
elf = '.pio/build/esp32-s3-devkitc-1/firmware.elf'
`
Tells Wokwi where to load compiled firmware from.

### diagram.json
`json
{
  \"version\": 1,
  \"author\": \"CoCIS Room 1\",
  \"editor\": \"wokwi\",
  \"parts\": [
    { \"type\": \"board-esp32-s3-devkitc-1\", \"id\": \"esp\", \"top\": 0, \"left\": 0, \"attrs\": {} },
    { \"type\": \"wokwi-pir-motion-sensor\", \"id\": \"pir1\", \"top\": -90, \"left\": 260, \"attrs\": {} },
    { \"type\": \"wokwi-led\", \"id\": \"led1\", \"top\": 100, \"left\": 260, \"attrs\": { \"color\": \"red\" } },
    { \"type\": \"wokwi-resistor\", \"id\": \"r1\", \"top\": 160, \"left\": 260, \"attrs\": { \"value\": \"220\" } }
  ],
  \"connections\": [
    [\"pir1:VCC\", \"esp:3V3\", \"red\", []],
    [\"pir1:GND\", \"esp:GND.1\", \"black\", []],
    [\"pir1:OUT\", \"esp:4\", \"green\", []],
    [\"esp:2\", \"r1:1\", \"green\", []],
    [\"r1:2\", \"led1:A\", \"green\", []],
    [\"led1:C\", \"esp:GND.1\", \"black\", []]
  ],
  \"dependencies\": {}
}
`
Connections: PIR OUT->GPIO4, LED via 220Ω on GPIO2.

## Build command from terminal (you tried pio --help)
You ran pio --help from D:\cocis-smart-system>. To build this specific project, you must be IN the project folder.

Option 1: Change directory
`powershell
cd D:\cocis-smart-system\room1
pio run
`

Option 2: Build with PlatformIO extension (easier) - Ctrl+Shift+P -> PlatformIO: Build

PlatformIO extension uses pio run under the hood. When you ran pio from parent folder with no platformio.ini, it just showed help - that is correct.

## Step by step to build & run
1. Open VS Code -> Open Folder -> D:\cocis-smart-system\room1
2. Ctrl+Shift+P -> PlatformIO: Build
3. Wait for SUCCESS
4. F1 -> Wokwi: Start Simulator
5. Click PIR sensor to trigger motion, wait 15s for timeout

## Common mistakes
- Building from wrong folder (parent folder) -> pio run gives help
- Using Arduino framework instead of espidf
- Wrong pins (GPIO4/GPIO2)
- Timeout too short for test

## Quick check
After build, verify:
`powershell
Get-ChildItem .pio\build\esp32-s3-devkitc-1\ -File | Where-Object { .Name -match \"firmware|elf\" }
`

## Learning questions (test yourself)
1. Why create a task instead of doing everything in app_main loop?
2. Why use 200ms sampling?
3. Why log only on transition?
4. What is xTaskGetTickCount() used for?
